# ---------- Config & secrets - never commit real values ----------
# Checked in: appsettings.json (the non-secret baseline) and
# appsettings.Development.json (shared dev defaults, log levels only).
# Not checked in: Production / Staging / local overrides - those values come
# from environment variables or a secret store at deploy time.
# Anything sensitive in development belongs in user secrets, never in
# appsettings.Development.json, which IS committed.
# Note: "appsettings.*.json" requires text between two dots, so it never
# matches "appsettings.json" itself - no negation is needed for that file.
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.Development.json

# User secrets ("dotnet user-secrets" keeps these outside the repo entirely;
# this is belt and braces).
secrets.json

# API keys / env files. ".env.*" does not match a bare ".env", so the plain
# filename is listed separately.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.secret
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem

# Azure / VS tooling output that can carry endpoints, connection strings and
# deploy credentials.
*.pubxml
*.pubxml.user
*.azurePubxml
*.publishsettings
*.publishproj
